WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.840
Hi everyone, today I would like to talk about Creator Connections, an easy to use tool that's designed

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.609
to generate additional sales for you.

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:20.840
It's under Amazon's advertising and brand content.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.821
There are a few easy steps to set it up.

00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:25.000
The first tip I want to give is the length of

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:25.582
the campaign.

00:00:25.582 --> 00:00:30.240
I would usually start a campaign for at least 3 to 6 months long because that

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.640
tells the creators that they actually have enough time to submit content and enough time

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.864
for them to generate sales for you.

00:00:36.864 --> 00:00:38.769
The second would be the budget.

00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:40.040
Honestly, I would really

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.915
suggest maximize your budget number.

00:00:41.915 --> 00:00:44.540
It can go up to crazy number.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.040
Usually, I only ended

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.600
up using a fraction of that budget, but again, that sends a very positive signal to creators

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.680
that you are in Creator Connections for a long haul and you have enough budget for your

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.004
campaign.

00:00:55.004 --> 00:00:57.594
And then the third would be commission rate.

00:00:57.594 --> 00:00:59.860
I would suggest starting from 10% at

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:00.224
least.

00:01:00.224 --> 00:01:04.956
Depending on how competitive your niche is, say my niche is super competitive.

00:01:04.956 --> 00:01:05.320
Sometimes

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:08.314
I go up to 20% as a commission rate.

00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:10.975
And then fourth would be the campaign brief.

00:01:10.975 --> 00:01:11.640
The information

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.630
in there would often be referred by the creator in their videos.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.960
So they're important, but

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.360
don't make it longer than a paragraph because anything longer than that, a lot of creators

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.089
they would just tune out.

00:01:23.089 --> 00:01:27.240
And then when creators messages you for samples, I usually ask my

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:32.080
VA to ask them for links of at least one of their social media platforms so that we can

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:32.600
check engagement.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.240
Not just the number of followers they have, but how many comments, how many

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.946
likes, and how often do they post on their platform?

00:01:38.946 --> 00:01:40.840
Those are all metrics for us to

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.687
determine if this creator is a good fit for us.

00:01:43.687 --> 00:01:45.680
And once they submitted the content and

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:51.880
generate some sales for you, definitely, definitely generate a list of effective creators who

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:57.080
has converted for you and who has submitted good content that fits your brand, you could

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.136
see it from the dashboard what kind of content they submitted.

00:02:00.136 --> 00:02:01.802
There is a link to that.

00:02:01.802 --> 00:02:02.080
So

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.960
there's really a lot of information you can see to determine how a creator can help you

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.880
generate sales the next time when you have a new campaign, definitely send messages to

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.800
invite those effective creators first and really prioritize them in terms of communicating

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:17.751
and sending samples.

00:02:17.751 --> 00:02:20.606
So that's my list of tips for Creator Connections.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:21.240
Happy selling.
